      ":question/id": "88e0b1bd-ab5b-5056-934f-dc0524e7e997",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-341147",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ for $f(x)={log}_{4}\u2061x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x.$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}\u2061x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}\u2061x)\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{log}_{4}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{log}_{4}\u2061x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}-\\frac{{log}_{4}\u2061x}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
