      ":question/id": "7013dfd6-3ee9-5a67-9438-689c7906b87e",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-31903",
      ":question/problem": "Find the slope of the tangent line to the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{3}-6x)$ at $x=1.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{3}-6x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-6x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032}(1)\\text{\u00a0} & =\\frac{3(1)^{2}-6}{|{1}^{3}-6(1)|\\sqrt{({1}^{3}-6(1))^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{|-5|\\sqrt{(1-6)^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{4\\cdot 6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{10\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{10\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{60} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
